d","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","review_id":"3jy_NeHlVU83rJp2L9jAow","date":"2014-12-09T19:50:32","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9312084913253784,"text_excerpt":"This place is pretty unassuming, I walked by it several times without going in. Once I did I was glad I have it a shot and have been back several times. The long and short: 1. Outdoor seating. Great large outdoor area, perfect for brunch and/or tailgating. Dogs are welcome (wait staff will bring out water bowls if asked). 2. Breakfast/Brunch. I like their brunch menu more than their lunch/dinner menu (which is not so different from other bar/grills). They make a mean eggs Benedict, the Cajun Be edict being my favorite thing on the menu. Bottomless mimosas are also available. 3. Bottomless mimosas. 1 mimosa will run you $5 and take about 30 seconds to drink while bottomless will run you $1..."},{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","review_id":"qMDkdbsC1tAzysWIOfmeag","date":"2016-06-28T21:54:28","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9265192151069641,"text_excerpt":"I remember this place once upon a time as the sand volleyball Hotspot, Polynesian Joe's, pre Hurricane Katrina. I came here for the first time in 13 years Sunday. The inside has not changed too much but the volleyball courts have been replaced with a large beautiful courtyard. We planned a trip to the nearby WWII Museum and decided to stop here for Sunday brunch. The brunch menu was a good size and had many good selections. The portions are pretty big. I had the chicken and waffles which were yummy. My tablemate had the French toast. He couldn't even come close to finishing it. Two people could probably split it. They do offer bottomless mimosas for $12. Friendly service and good atmosphe..."},{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","review_id":"2bDhjhNFAs6ekGSiWcACwQ","date":"2014-03-26T17:57:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.925973653793335,"text_excerpt":"This place is really great and so much better than the horrible MsGuires that used to be located here. Our waitress was really fantastic. Her name is Stephanie and she was so very attentive to our needs. She even let us take one of the unlmited bloody mary's to go :) I ordered the crawfish quesadillas, which I will admit were not very good mainly because they were too fishy and i dont think the crawfish were cooked right. But my friend has the lamb sliders and they were awesome! Love the ambience and courtyard here. Perfect place for happy hour after work during the nice weather months,"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","photo_id":"LBdAny9Z6A-Ku5xV8UtKUw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/LBdAny9Z6A-Ku5xV8UtKUw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9403140544891357},{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","photo_id":"puDRjPDHaSJWwoWuGxR3aw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/puDRjPDHaSJWwoWuGxR3aw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9042169451713562},{"business_id":"WENbCl6Z11qLfmolyOfaeg","photo_id":"rsaQ9O0LMlH874zFAWqwvw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/rsaQ9O0LMlH874zFAWqwvw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8629571795463562}]},"notebook_case":null}
